ssage_type":"next","turn_exchange_id":"ce6ec6a2-5bbc-4770-906e-33ca35cdb639","working_turn_id":"ce6ec6a2-5bbc-4770-906e-33ca35cdb639","model_slug":"gpt-6","default_model_slug":"gpt-6","parent_id":"6eab5df2-44ba-4b31-a9dd-8a69398a67c5","logical_answer_prefix_activity":{"visibility":"hidden"},"model_switcher_deny":[],"can_save":false},"recipient":"all","channel":"final"},{"id":"8e73e884-ca53-49b7-bd26-fe28b7930327","author":{"role":"assistant","name":null,"metadata":{}},"create_time":1792299635.513693,"update_time":1792299635.513693,"content":{"content_type":"reasoning_recap","content":"思考了 15s"},"status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":false,"weight":1.0,"metadata":{"reasoning_status":"reasoning_ended","finished_duration_sec":15,"reasoning_start_time":1792299619.5693617,"reasoning_end_time":1792299635.4925487,"reasoning_recap_type":"hide_all","cot_version":"v5","reasoning_group_id":"dca74887-37ce-4174-b5e7-1ff251be7b29","conversation_followup_suggestions_eligible":false,"request_id":"3f6b3021-f249-4ac9-90cb-b11c69cd445f","message_type":"next","turn_exchange_id":"ce6ec6a2-5bbc-4770-906e-33ca35cdb639","working_turn_id":"ce6ec6a2-5bbc-4770-906e-33ca35cdb639","model_slug":"gpt-6","default_model_slug":"gpt-6","can_save":false,"parent_id":"28651447-8be1-4861-bc57-8f1e745f8d57","hide_inline_actions":true,"model_switcher_deny":[]},"recipient":"all","channel":null},{"id":"fc74ff5e-52db-4463-8fa4-d43780dfdd5c","author":{"role":"assistant","name":null,"metadata":{}},"create_time":1792299635.527498,"update_time":1792299778.903337,"content":{"content_type":"code","language":"unknown","response_format_name":null,"text":"from pathlib import Path\nimport textwrap, zipfile, os, json\n\nroot = Path(\"/mnt/data/evoagent-comic-studio-v0.1\")\nif root.exists():\n    import shutil\n    shutil.rmtree(root)\nroot.mkdir(parents=True)\n\nfiles = {\n\"README.md\": r\"\"\"\n# EvoAgent Comic Studio V0.1\n\nA runnable MVP for a 30–60 second AI comic-drama pipeline. It includes a deterministic/mock end-to-end path, SQLite asset/task tracking, a DAG runner, FFmpeg assembly, quality checks, budget gates, failure records, and a guarded evolution proposal workflow.\n\n## What actually runs now\n\n- Python CLI and SQLite persistence.\n- Project creation and a 3-scene storyboard (mock planner).\n- Task DAG execution with dependency tracking.\n- SRT subtitle generation.\n- FFmpeg-based local video assembly using generated color-card placeholder scenes and silent audio. This validates timeline, encoding, and delivery mechanics without paid APIs.\n- Quality gates: output exists, duration bounds, video stream exists, subtitle file exists.\n- Budget gate and JSONL event log.\n- Candidate config evaluation and guarded promotion of low-risk config values.\n\n## What requires a real external provider\n\nThe default `mock` provider does **not** generate actual anime artwork, motion video, or natural speech. It creates placeholder clips and subtitle text so the complete pipeline can be exercised locally.\n\nTo produce real content, implement provider adapters for:\n- image generation (character reference / scene keyframes)\n- image-to-video or text-to-video generation\n- TTS / voice generation\n- optionally an LLM script/storyboard planner\n\nProvider adapters should return local asset paths and metadata, and must implement idempotency, timeout, retry and cost reporting. Do not place provider API keys in source files.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- Python 3.11+\n- FFmpeg and ffprobe installed and on PATH\n- No Python third-party packages required for the mock MVP\n\nVerify:\n```bash\npython --version\nffmpeg -version\nffprobe -version\n```\n\n## Run\n\n```bash\npython -m evoagent_comic init --workspace ./workspace\npython -m evoagent_comic run --workspace ./workspace --title \"The Exiled Star\" --duration 45\npython -m evoagent_comic status --workspace ./workspace\npython -m evoagent_comic evaluate --workspace ./workspace\n```\n\nOutput:\n- `workspace/projects/<project_id>/project.json`\n- `workspace/projects/<project_id>/assets/`\n- `workspace/projects/<project_id>/output/final.mp4`\n- `workspace/projects/<project_id>/output/subtitles.srt`\n- `workspace/evoagent.sqlite3`\n- `workspace/events.jsonl`\n\nTo inspect all tasks:\n```bash\npython -m evoagent_comic tasks --workspace ./workspace\n```\n\n## Pipeline DAG\n\n`brief -> script -> character_bible -> storyboard -> scene_assets -> voice_assets -> subtitles -> assemble -> quality_gate -> deliver`\n\nThe MVP runs sequentially in topological order. Production adapters may fan out `scene_assets` and `voice_assets` by scene, with concurrency limits.\n\n## Budget policy\n\nThe mock provider reports zero external generation cost. In `config.toml`, set a project budget and per-task ceilings before enabling paid adapters. Cost must be reserved before submitting a billable request, then reconciled against provider-reported actual cost.\n\n## Stable vs evolution track\n\n- Stable path: `config.toml` and the current CLI runtime.\n- Evolution path: `experiments/` and `evolution/` records.\n- Only allowlisted configuration keys may be proposed automatically.\n- Code changes, tool implementation changes, permissions, and provider credentials are not eligible for automatic promotion in V0.1.\n- Promotion writes a new config version and audit record; it does not mutate Python code.\n\n## Known MVP limitations\n\n- The generated scenes are placeholders, not real anime footage.\n- Character consistency is represented by a character bible and reference asset metadata; semantic visual consistency needs a real vision evaluator and real image/video providers.\n- The QC checks are deterministic technical checks, not subjective story/acting quality evaluation.\n- The CLI backend is ready to be wrapped by FastAPI for Android integration, but the API server is not included in V0.1.\n\"\"\",\n\"pyproject.toml\": r\"\"\"\n[build-system]\nrequires = [\"setuptools>=68\"]\nbuild-backend = \"setuptools.build_meta\"\n\n[project]\nname = \"evoagent-comic-studio\"\nversion = \"0.1.0\"\ndescription = \"Runnable MVP for an AI comic-drama production pipeline\"\nrequires-python = \">=3.11\"\ndependencies = []\n\n[project.scripts]\nevo-comic = \"evoagent_comic.cli:main\"\n\n[tool.setuptools.packages.find]\nwhere = [\".\"]\ninclude = [\"evoagent_comic*\"]\n\"\"\",\n\".gitignore\": r\"\"\"\n.venv/\n__pycache__/\n*.py[cod]\nworkspace/\n.env\n\"\"\",\n\"config.toml\": r\"\"\"\n[project]\ndefault_duration_seconds = 45\nmin_duration_seconds = 30\nmax_duration_seconds = 60\nfps = 24\nwidth = 1280\nheight = 720\nscene_count = 3\n\n[budget]\ntotal_usd = 5.00\nimage_generation_usd = 1.00\nvideo_generation_usd = 3.00\ntts_usd = 0.50\nllm_usd = 0.50\nreserve_before_call = true\n\n[providers]\nplanner = \"mock\"\nimage = \"mock\"\nvideo = \"mock\"\ntts = \"mock\"\n\n[quality]\nmin_duration_seconds = 30\nmax_duration_seconds = 60\nrequire_subtitles = true\nrequire_audio_stream = true\nallow_placeholder_media = true\n\n[evolution]\nauto_promote_low_risk_config = false\nminimum_eval_cases = 3\nminimum_score = 0.80\nallowlisted_keys = [\"project.scene_count\", \"project.fps\"]\n\"\"\",\n\"evoagent_comic/__init__.py\": r\"\"\"\n__version__ = \"0.1.0\"\n\"\"\",\n\"evoagent_comic/__main__.py\": r\"\"\"\nfrom .cli import main\nmain()\n\"\"\",\n\"evoagent_comic/models.py\": r\"\"\"\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass, asdict\nfrom typing import Any\nimport time\nimport uuid\n\ndef new_id(prefix: str) -> str:\n    return f\"{prefix}_{uuid.uuid4().hex[:12]}\"\n\n@dataclass\nclass Task:\n    task_id: str\n    project_id: str\n    name: str\n    status: str = \"pending\"\n    dependencies: list[str] | None = None\n    attempts: int = 0\n    error: str | None = None\n    output_json: str | None = None\n    started_at: float | None = None\n    finished_at: float | None = None\n\n@dataclass\nclass Asset:\n    asset_id: str\n    project_id: str\n    kind: str\n    path: str\n    version: int = 1\n    checksum: str | None = None\n    metadata: dict[str, Any] | None = None\n    status: str = \"ready\"\n    created_at: float = 0.0\n\n@dataclass\nclass Event:\n    event_id: str\n    project_id: str\n    task_id: str | None\n    event_type: str\n    payload: dict[str, Any]\n    timestamp: float = 0.0\n\ndef now() -> float:\n    return time.time()\n\"\"\",\n\"evoagent_comic/db.py\": r\"\"\"\nimport json, sqlite3, time\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom .models import new_id\n\nSCHEMA = '''\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS projects(\n project_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, title TEXT NOT NULL, duration_seconds INTEGER NOT NULL,\n status TEXT NOT NULL, created_at REAL NOT NULL, config_json TEXT NOT NULL\n);\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS tasks(\n task_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, project_id TEXT NOT NULL, name TEXT NOT NULL,\n status TEXT NOT NULL, dependencies_json TEXT NOT NULL, attempts INTEGER NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n error TEXT, output_json TEXT, started_at REAL, finished_at REAL,\n FOREIGN KEY(project_id) REFERENCES projects(project_id)\n);\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS assets(\n asset_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, project_id TEXT NOT NULL, kind TEXT NOT NULL, path TEXT NOT NULL,\n version INTEGER NOT NULL, checksum TEXT, metadata_json TEXT NOT NULL, status TEXT NOT NULL,\n created_at REAL NOT NULL, FOREIGN KEY(project_id) REFERENCES projects(project_id)\n);\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS events(\n event_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, project_id TEXT NOT NULL, task_id TEXT, event_type TEXT NOT NULL,\n payload_json TEXT NOT NULL, timestamp REAL NOT NULL\n);\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS issues(\n issue_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, project_id TEXT NOT NULL, task_id TEXT, category TEXT NOT NULL,\n severity TEXT NOT NULL, suspected_component TEXT NOT NULL, evidence_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n status TEXT NOT NULL, created_at REAL NOT NULL\n);\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS experiments(\n experiment_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, project_id TEXT, title TEXT NOT NULL, candidate_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n baseline_score REAL, candidate_score REAL, status TEXT NOT NULL, report_json TEXT NOT NULL,\n created_at REAL NOT NULL\n);\nCREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS budgets(\n project_id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, limit_usd REAL NOT NULL, reserved_usd REAL NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n actual_usd REAL NOT NULL DEFAULT 0, FOREIGN KEY(project_id) REFERENCES projects(project_id)\n);\n'''\n\nclass Store:\n    def __init__(self, workspace: Path):\n        self.workspace = workspace\n        self.workspace.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        self.db_path = workspace / \"evoagent.sqlite3\"\n        with self.connect() as c:\n            c.executescript(SCHEMA)\n\n    def connect(self):\n        c = sqlite3.connect(self.db_path)\n        c.row_factory = sqlite3.Row\n        return c\n\n    def create_project(self, project_id, title, duration, config):\n        with self.connect() as c:\n            c.execute(\"INSERT INTO projects VALUES(?,?,?,?,?,?)\",\n                      (project_id, title, duration, \"running\", time.time(), json.dumps(config)))\n            c.execute(\"INSERT INTO budgets(project_id,limit_usd) VALUES(?,?)\",\n                      (project_id, float(config.get(\"budget\", {}).get(\"total_usd\", 5.0))))\n\n    def add_task(self, project_id, name, deps):\n        task_id = new_id(\"task\")\n        with self.connect() as c:\n            c.execute(\"INSERT INTO tasks(task_id,project_id,name,status,dependencies_json) VALUES(?,?,?,?,?)\",\n                      (task_id, project_id, name, \"pending\", json.dumps(deps)))\n        return task_id\n\n    def task_by_name(self, project_id, name):\n        with self.connect() as c:\n            r = c.execute(\"SELECT * FROM tasks WHERE project_id=? AND name=?\", (project_id, name)).fetchone()\n        return dict(r) if r else None\n\n    def update_task(self, task_id, **fields):\n        allowed = {\"status\",\"attempts\",\"error\",\"output_json\",\"started_at\",\"finished_at\"}\n        fields = {k:v for k,v in fields.items() if k in allowed}\n        if not fields: return\n        sql = \"UPDATE tasks SET \" + \",\".join(f\"{k}=?\" for k in fields) + \" WHERE task_id=?\"\n        with self.connect() as c:\n            c.execute(sql, [*fields.values(), task_id])\n\n    def tasks(self, project_id=None):\n        with self.connect() as c:\n            if project_id:\n                rows = c.execute(\"SELECT * FROM tasks WHERE project_id=? ORDER BY rowid\", (project_id,)).fetchall()\n            else:\n                rows = c.execute(\"SELECT * FROM tasks ORDER BY rowid DESC\").fetchall()\n        return [dict(r) for r in rows]\n\n    def add_asset(self, project_id, kind, path, metadata=None, version=1, status=\"ready\"):\n        import hashlib\n        p = Path(path)\n        checksum = hashlib.sha256(p.read_bytes()).hexdigest() if p.exists() and p.is_file() else None\n        asset_id = new_id(\"asset\")\n        with self.connect() as c:\n            c.execute(\"INSERT INTO assets VALUES(?,?,?,?,?,?,?,?,?)\",\n                      (asset_id, project_id, kind, str(p), version, checksum,\n                       json.dumps(metadata or {}), status, time.time()))\n        return asset_id\n\n    def assets(self, project_id):\n        with self.connect() as c:\n            rows = c.execute(\"SELECT * FROM assets WHERE project_id=? ORDER BY created_at\", (project_id,)).fetchall()\n        return [dict(r) for r in rows]\n\n    def event(self, workspace, project_id, event_type, payload, task_id=None):\n        event = {\"event_id\": new_id(\"evt\"), \"project_id\": project_id, \"task_id\": task_id,\n                 \"event_type\": event_type, \"payload\": payload, \"timestamp\": time.time()}\n        with self.connect() as c:\n            c.execute(\"INSERT INTO events VALUES(?,?,?,?,?,?)\",\n                      (event[\"event_id\"], project_id, task_id, event_type, json.dumps(payload), event[\"timestamp\"]))\n        with (workspace / \"events.jsonl\").open(\"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as f:\n            f.write(json.dumps(event, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n\n    def issue(self, project_id, task_id, category, severity, component, evidence):\n        with self.connect() as c:\n            c.execute(\"INSERT INTO issues VALUES(?,?,?,?,?,?,?,?,?)\",\n                      (new_id(\"issue\"), project_id, task_id, category, severity, component,\n                       json.dumps(evidence), \"open\", time.time()))\n\n    def budget(self, project_id):\n        with self.connect() as c:\n            r = c.execute(\"SELECT * FROM budgets WHERE project_id=?\", (project_id,)).fetchone()\n        return dict(r) if r else None\n\n    def reserve_budget(self, project_id, amount):\n        with self.connect() as c:\n            r = c.execute(\"SELECT * FROM budgets WHERE project_id=?\", (project_id,)).fetchone()\n            if not r or r[\"actual_usd\"] + r[\"reserved_usd\"] + amount > r[\"limit_usd\"]:\n                return False\n            c.execute(\"UPDATE budgets SET reserved_usd=reserved_usd+? WHERE project_id=?\", (amount, project_id))\n            return True\n\n    def settle_budget(self, project_id, reserved, actual):\n        with self.connect() as c:\n            c.execute(\"UPDATE budgets SET reserved_usd=MAX(0,reserved_usd-?), actual_usd=actual_usd+? WHERE project_id=?\",\n                      (reserved, actual, project_id))\n\n    def finish_project(self, project_id, status):\n        with self.connect() as c:\n            c.execute(\"UPDATE projects SET status=? WHERE project_id=?\", (status, project_id))\n\n    def projects(self):\n        with self.connect() as c:\n            return [dict(r) for r in c.execute(\"SELECT * FROM projects ORDER BY created_at DESC\").fetchall()]\n\"\"\",\n\"evoagent_comic/config.py\": r\"\"\"\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport tomllib\n\nDEFAULT_CONFIG = {\n \"project\":{\"default_duration_seconds\":45,\"min_duration_seconds\":30,\"max_duration_seconds\":60,\n            \"fps\":24,\"width\":1280,\"height\":720,\"scene_count\":3},\n \"budget\":{\"total_usd\":5.0,\"image_generation_usd\":1.0,\"video_generation_usd\":3.0,\n           \"tts_usd\":0.5,\"llm_usd\":0.5,\"reserve_before_call\":True},\n \"providers\":{\"planner\":\"mock\",\"image\":\"mock\",\"video\":\"mock\",\"tts\":\"mock\"},\n \"quality\":{\"min_duration_seconds\":30,\"max_duration_seconds\":60,\"require_subtitles\":True,\n            \"require_audio_stream\":True,\"allow_placeholder_media\":True},\n \"evolution\":{\"auto_promote_low_risk_config\":False,\"minimum_eval_cases\":3,\"minimum_score\":0.8,\n              \"allowlisted_keys\":[\"project.scene_count\",\"project.fps\"]}\n}\n\ndef load_config(path: Path | None = None):\n    path = path or Path(\"config.toml\")\n    if not path.exists():\n        return DEFAULT_CONFIG.copy()\n    with path.open(\"rb\") as f:\n        cfg = tomllib.load(f)\n    merged = {k: dict(v) if isinstance(v, dict) else v for k,v in DEFAULT_CONFIG.items()}\n    for k,v in cfg.items():\n        if isinstance(v, dict) and k in merged: merged[k].update(v)\n        else: merged[k] = v\n    return merged\n\"\"\",\n\"evoagent_comic/providers.py\": r\"\"\"\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json, subprocess, textwrap, wave, struct, math\n\nclass MockPlanner:\n    def create_script(self, title, duration, scene_count):\n        return {\n            \"title\": title,\n            \"logline\": \"A discarded young cultivator discovers a hidden power and turns the tables.\",\n            \"characters\": [\n                {\"id\":\"hero\",\"name\":\"Lin Yan\",\"visual_anchor\":\"young anime man, black hair, silver-blue eyes, dark robe with one torn sleeve\"},\n                {\"id\":\"rival\",\"name\":\"Elder's Heir\",\"visual_anchor\":\"tall anime man, white-gold robe, jade hair ornament, cold expression\"}\n            ],\n            \"scenes\": [\n                {\"id\":f\"scene_{i+1:02d}\",\"duration_seconds\":duration/scene_count,\n                 \"location\":loc,\"beat\":beat,\"visual_prompt\":prompt,\"dialogue\":dialogue}\n                for i,(loc,beat,prompt,dialogue) in enumerate([\n                    (\"sect courtyard\",\"humiliation\",\"anime fantasy sect courtyard at dusk, young exiled cultivator kneeling in rain, dramatic wide shot\",\"Rival: You are no longer one of us.\"),\n                    (\"stone steps\",\"awakening\",\"close-up of the young cultivator's silver-blue eyes glowing, dark fantasy energy swirling, cinematic anime lighting\",\"Hero: Then I will carve my own path.\"),\n                    (\"mountain gate\",\"reversal\",\"young cultivator stands as blue lightning cracks the sky, rival recoils, epic anime cliffhanger\",\"Narrator: That day, the abandoned star awakened.\")\n                ][:scene_count])\n            ]\n        }\n\nclass MockMediaProvider:\n    \"\"\"Creates placeholder media for pipeline testing; not actual AI-generated art.\"\"\"\n    def create_scene_clip(self, output: Path, duration: float, width: int, height: int, fps: int, index: int):\n        colors = [\"0x18253F\", \"0x3A1F4B\", \"0x153C49\", \"0x4A2630\"]\n        color = colors[(index-1) % len(colors)]\n        cmd = [\n            \"ffmpeg\",\"-y\",\"-hide_banner\",\"-loglevel\",\"error\",\n            \"-f\",\"lavfi\",\"-i\",f\"color=c={color}:s={width}x{height}:r={fps}:d={duration}\",\n            \"-f\",\"lavfi\",\"-i\",\"anullsrc=channel_layout=stereo:sample_rate=44100\",\n            \"-shortest\",\"-c:v\",\"libx264\",\"-pix_fmt\",\"yuv420p\",\"-c:a\",\"aac\",\n            \"-t\",str(duration),str(output)\n        ]\n        subprocess.run(cmd, check=True, capture_output=True, text=True)\n\n    def create_tts_placeholder(self, output: Path, duration: float):\n        # Quiet placeholder WAV tone/silence to exercise the audio path; replace with real TTS.\n        rate = 22050\n        n = int(rate * duration)\n        with wave.open(str(output), \"wb\") as w:\n            w.setnchannels(1); w.setsampwidth(2); w.setframerate(rate)\n            frames = bytearray()\n            for i in range(n):\n                val = int(180 * math.sin(2*math.pi*220*i/rate)) if i < rate*0.08 else 0\n                frames.extend(struct.pack(\"<h\", val))\n            w.writeframes(frames)\n\nclass ExternalProviderNotConfigured(RuntimeError):\n    pass\n\nclass ExternalProviderAdapter:\n    \"\"\"Contract placeholder. Implement provider-specific API calls in a separate adapter.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, name: str, api_key_env: str):\n        self.name, self.api_key_env = name, api_key_env\n    def generate(self, **kwargs):\n        raise ExternalProviderNotConfigured(\n            f\"Provider '{self.name}' is not implemented. Add API adapter, auth, timeout, idempotency, and cost reconciliation.\"\n        )\n\"\"\",\n\"evoagent_comic/dag.py\": r\"\"\"\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom typing import Callable\n\n@dataclass\nclass DagNode:\n    name: str\n    dependencies: list[str]\n    run: Callable[[], dict]\n\nclass DagRunner:\n    def __init__(self, nodes: list[DagNode]):\n        self.nodes = {n.name:n for n in nodes}\n\n    def order(self):\n        result, temporary, permanent = [], set(), set()\n        def visit(name):\n            if name in permanent: return\n            if name in temporary: raise ValueError(f\"DAG cycle detected at {name}\")\n            if name not in self.nodes: raise ValueError(f\"Unknown dependency: {name}\")\n            temporary.add(name)\n            for dep in self.nodes[name].dependencies: visit(dep)\n            temporary.remove(name); permanent.add(name); result.append(name)\n        for name in self.nodes: visit(name)\n        return result\n\n    def run(self, on_start=None, on_success=None, on_failure=None):\n        results = {}\n        for name in self.order():\n            node = self.nodes[name]\n            if on_start: on_start(name, node.dependencies)\n            try:\n                results[name] = node.run()\n                if on_success: on_success(name, results[name])\n            except Exception as e:\n                if on_failure: on_failure(name, e)\n                raise\n        return results\n\"\"\",\n\"evoagent_comic/pipeline.py\": r\"\"\"\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport json, subprocess, time, shutil, textwrap\nfrom .models import new_id\nfrom .providers import MockPlanner, MockMediaProvider\nfrom .dag import DagNode, DagRunner\n\ndef _write_json(path, data):\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    path.write_text(json.dumps(data, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\ndef _probe(path):\n    cmd = [\"ffprobe\",\"-v\",\"error\",\"-show_entries\",\"format=duration:stream=codec_type,width,height\",\"-of\",\"json\",str(path)]\n    out = subprocess.run(cmd, check=True, capture_output=True, text=True)\n    return json.loads(out.stdout)\n\ndef _srt_time(seconds):\n    ms = int(round(seconds * 1000))\n    h, ms = divmod(ms, 3600000); m, ms = divmod(ms, 60000); s, ms = divmod(ms, 1000)\n    return f\"{h:02}:{m:02}:{s:02},{ms:03}\"\n\nclass ComicPipeline:\n    def __init__(self, workspace, store, config):\n        self.workspace, self.store, self.config = workspace, store, config\n        self.planner = MockPlanner()\n        self.media = MockMediaProvider()\n\n    def run(self, title, duration):\n        p = self.config[\"project\"]\n        if not (p[\"min_duration_seconds\"] <= duration <= p[\"max_duration_seconds\"]):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Duration must be between {p['min_duration_seconds']} and {p['max_duration_seconds']} seconds\")\n        project_id = new_id(\"comic\")\n        base = self.workspace / \"projects\" / project_id\n        assets, output = base / \"assets\", base / \"output\"\n        assets.mkdir(parents=True); output.mkdir(parents=True)\n        project = {\"project_id\":project_id,\"title\":title,\"duration_seconds\":duration,\n                   \"status\":\"running\",\"provider_mode\":\"mock\",\"created_at\":time.time()}\n        _write_json(base/\"project.json\", project)\n        self.store.create_project(project_id,title,duration,self.config)\n        self.store.event(self.workspace,project_id,\"project.created\",project)\n\n        task_deps = {\n          \"brief\": [],\n          \"script\": [\"brief\"],\n          \"character_bible\": [\"script\"],\n          \"storyboard\": [\"character_bible\"],\n          \"scene_assets\": [\"storyboard\"],\n          \"voice_assets\": [\"storyboard\"],\n          \"subtitles\": [\"script\",\"voice_assets\"],\n          \"assemble\": [\"scene_assets\",\"subtitles\"],\n          \"quality_gate\": [\"assemble\"],\n          \"deliver\": [\"quality_gate\"]\n        }\n        for name,deps in task_deps.items(): self.store.add_task(project_id,name,deps)\n\n        def task(name, fn):\n            def wrapped():\n                row = self.store.task_by_name(project_id,name)\n                self.store.update_task(row[\"task_id\"],status=\"running\",started_at=time.time(),attempts=row[\"attempts\"]+1)\n                self.store.event(self.workspace,project_id,\"task.started\",{\"name\":name},row[\"task_id\"])\n                try:\n                    result = fn()\n                    self.store.update_task(row[\"task_id\"],status=\"succeeded\",finished_at=time.time(),output_json=json.dumps(result))\n                    self.store.event(self.workspace,project_id,\"task.succeeded\",{\"name\":name,\"result\":result},row[\"task_id\"])\n                    return result\n                except Exception as e:\n                    self.store.update_task(row[\"task_id\"],status=\"failed\",error=str(e),finished_at=time.time())\n                    self.store.issue(project_id,row[\"task_id\"],\"pipeline_failure\",\"high\",name,{\"error\":str(e)})\n                    self.store.event(self.workspace,project_id,\"task.failed\",{\"name\":name,\"error\":str(e)},row[\"task_id\"])\n                    raise\n            return wrapped\n\n        def brief():\n            data={\"title\":title,\"duration_seconds\":duration,\"genre\":\"fantasy action\",\"tone\":\"dramatic cliffhanger\",\n                  \"target\":\"30-60 second verticalizable short; MVP output is 16:9 landscape\"}\n            _write_json(assets/\"brief.json\",data); self.store.add_asset(project_id,\"brief\",assets/\"brief.json\",data)\n            return data\n\n        def script():\n            data=self.planner.create_script(title,duration,p[\"scene_count\"])\n            _write_json(assets/\"script.json\",data); self.store.add_asset(project_id,\"script\",assets/\"script.json\",{\"provider\":\"mock\"})\n            return {\"scene_count\":len(data[\"scenes\"]),\"characters\":len(data[\"characters\"]),\"provider\":\"mock\"}\n\n        def character_bible():\n            data=json.loads((assets/\"script.json\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))[\"characters\"]\n            out={\"version\":1,\"characters\":data,\"consistency_policy\":\"Reuse exact visual_anchor and reference assets in all real provider calls.\"}\n            _write_json(assets/\"character_bible.json\",out); self.store.add_asset(project_id,\"character_bible\",assets/\"character_bible.json\")\n            return {\"characters\":len(data)}\n\n        def storyboard():\n            data=json.loads((assets/\"script.json\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n            scenes=[]\n            start=0.0\n            for i,s in enumerate(data[\"scenes\"],1):\n                d=duration/len(data[\"scenes\"])\n                scenes.append({**s,\"shot_index\":i,\"start_seconds\":round(start,3),\"end_seconds\":round(start+d,3),\n                               \"required_checks\":[\"file_exists\",\"duration\",\"character_anchor\",\"subtitle_timing\"]})\n                start += d\n            out={\"version\":1,\"scenes\":scenes,\"fps\":p[\"fps\"],\"width\":p[\"width\"],\"height\":p[\"height\"]}\n            _write_json(assets/\"storyboard.json\",out); self.store.add_asset(project_id,\"storyboard\",assets/\"storyboard.json\")\n            return {\"shots\":len(scenes),\"fps\":p[\"fps\"]}\n\n        def scene_assets():\n            sb=json.loads((assets/\"storyboard.json\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n            clips=[]\n            for s in sb[\"scenes\"]:\n                clip=assets/f\"{s['id']}.mp4\"\n                self.media.create_scene_clip(clip,s[\"duration_seconds\"],p[\"width\"],p[\"height\"],p[\"fps\"],s[\"shot_index\"])\n                self.store.add_asset(project_id,\"scene_placeholder_video\",clip,{\"scene_id\":s[\"id\"],\"placeholder\":True})\n                clips.append(str(clip))\n            concat=assets/\"concat.txt\"\n            concat.write_text(\"\".join(f\"file '{Path(c).resolve().as_posix()}'\\n\" for c in clips),encoding=\"utf-8\")\n            return {\"clips\":clips,\"concat_file\":str(concat),\"placeholder\":True}\n\n        def voice_assets():\n            # Placeholder audio is deliberately not represented as natural speech.\n            voice=assets/\"voice_placeholder.wav\"\n            self.media.create_tts_placeholder(voice, duration)\n            self.store.add_asset(project_id,\"voice_placeholder_audio\",voice,{\"placeholder\":True,\"note\":\"Replace with actual TTS adapter\"})\n            return {\"audio\":str(voice),\"placeholder\":True}\n\n        def subtitles():\n            script_data=json.loads((assets/\"script.json\").read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n            per=duration/len(script_data[\"scenes\"]); lines=[]\n            for i,s in enumerate(script_data[\"scenes\"],1):\n                start=(i-1)*per; end=i*per\n                lines += [str(i),f\"{_srt_time(start)} --> {_srt_time(end)}\",s[\"dialogue\"],\"\"]\n            path=output/\"subtitles.srt\"; path.write_text(\"\\n\".join(lines),encoding=\"utf-8\")\n            self.store.add_asset(project_id,\"subtitles\",path,{\"format\":\"srt\",\"placeholder_dialogue\":True})\n            return {\"path\":str(path),\"entries\":len(script_data[\"scenes\"])}\n\n        def assemble():\n            concat=assets/\"concat.txt\"\n            silent=output/\"silent.mp4\"\n            subprocess.run([\"ffmpeg\",\"-y\",\"-hide_banner\",\"-loglevel\",\"error\",\"-f\",\"concat\",\"-safe\",\"0\",\"-i\",str(concat),\n                            \"-c\",\"copy\",str(silent)],check=True,capture_output=True,text=True)\n            voice=assets/\"voice_placeholder.wav\"\n            final=output/\"final.mp4\"\n            # Encode/mux audio and video. Placeholder audio is not real dialogue.\n            subprocess.run([\"ffmpeg\",\"-y\",\"-hide_banner\",\"-loglevel\",\"error\",\"-i\",str(silent),\"-i\",str(voice),\n                            \"-map\",\"0:v:0\",\"-map\",\"1:a:0\",\"-vf\",f\"scale={p['width']}:{p['height']},fps={p['fps']}\",\n                            \"-c:v\",\"libx264\",\"-pix_fmt\",\"yuv420p\",\"-c:a\",\"aac\",\"-shortest\",str(final)],\n                           check=True,capture_output=True,text=True)\n            self.store.add_asset(project_id,\"final_video\",final,{\"placeholder_media\":True,\"format\":\"mp4\"})\n            return {\"final_video\":str(final)}\n\n        def quality_gate():\n            final=output/\"final.mp4\"\n            probe=_probe(final)\n            dur=float(probe.get(\"format\",{}).get(\"duration\",0))\n            streams=probe.get(\"streams\",[])\n            has_video=any(s.get(\"codec_type\")==\"video\" for s in streams)\n            has_audio=any(s.get(\"codec_type\")==\"audio\" for s in streams)\n            checks={\n              \"file_exists\":final.exists() and final.stat().st_size>1024,\n              \"duration_in_range\":self.config[\"quality\"][\"min_duration_seconds\"] <= dur <= self.config[\"quality\"][\"max_duration_seconds\"],\n              \"video_stream\":has_video,\n              \"audio_stream\":has_audio if self.config[\"quality\"][\"require_audio_stream\"] else True,\n              \"subtitles_exist\":(output/\"subtitles.srt\").exists() if self.config[\"quality\"][\"require_subtitles\"] else True,\n              \"placeholder_warning\":True\n            }\n            report={\"passed\":all(v for k,v in checks.items() if k!=\"placeholder_warning\"),\"checks\":checks,\n                    \"duration_seconds\":dur,\"streams\":streams,\"note\":\"Technical checks only; this MVP uses placeholder media.\"}\n            _write_json(output/\"quality_report.json\",report); self.store.add_asset(project_id,\"quality_report\",output/\"quality_report.json\",report)\n            if not report[\"passed\"]: raise RuntimeError(f\"Quality gate failed: {checks}\")\n            return report\n\n        def deliver():\n            manifest={\"project_id\":project_id,\"title\":title,\"final_video\":str(output/\"final.mp4\"),\n                      \"subtitles\":str(output/\"subtitles.srt\"),\"quality_report\":str(output/\"quality_report.json\"),\n                      \"media_mode\":\"placeholder\",\"ready_for_real_provider_adapters\":True}\n            _write_json(output/\"delivery_manifest.json\",manifest)\n            self.store.add_asset(project_id,\"delivery_manifest\",output/\"delivery_manifest.json\",manifest)\n            self.store.finish_project(project_id,\"succeeded\")\n            return manifest\n\n        fns={\"brief\":brief,\"script\":script,\"character_bible\":character_bible,\"storyboard\":storyboard,\n             \"scene_assets\":scene_assets,\"voice_assets\":voice_assets,\"subtitles\":subtitles,\n             \"assemble\":assemble,\"quality_gate\":quality_gate,\"deliver\":deliver}\n        nodes=[DagNode(name,deps,task(name,fns[name])) for name,deps in task_deps.items()]\n        try:\n            results=DagRunner(nodes).run(\n                on_start=lambda n,d: print(f\"[RUN] {n} (depends on: {', '.join(d) or 'none'})\"),\n                on_success=lambda n,r: print(f\"[ OK ] {n}\"),\n                on_failure=lambda n,e: print(f\"[FAIL] {n}: {e}\")\n            )\n            project[\"status\"]=\"succeeded\"\n            _write_json(base/\"project.json\",project)\n            return {\"project_id\":project_id,\"project_dir\":str(base),\"output\":str(output/\"final.mp4\"),\"results\":results}\n        except Exception:\n            project[\"status\"]=\"failed\"; _write_json(base/\"project.json\",project)\n            self.store.finish_project(project_id,\"failed\")\n            raise\n\"\"\",\n\"evoagent_comic/evaluation.py\": r\"\"\"\nimport json, subprocess\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\ndef evaluate_project(project_dir: Path):\n    output = project_dir / \"output\"\n    final = output / \"final.mp4\"\n    report_path = output / \"quality_report.json\"\n    report = json.loads(report_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")) if report_path.exists() else {}\n    checks = report.get(\"checks\", {})\n    score = sum(1 for k,v in checks.items() if k != \"placeholder_warning\" and v) / max(1, sum(1 for k in checks if k != \"placeholder_warning\"))\n    return {\"project_dir\":str(project_dir),\"score\":round(score,3),\"passed\":bool(report.get(\"passed\",False)),\n            \"placeholder_media\":True,\"checks\":checks,\n            \"limitation\":\"This score measures technical pipeline checks, not story or visual quality.\"}\n\"\"\",\n\"evoagent_comic/evolution.py\": r\"\"\"\nimport json, time\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom .models import new_id\n\ndef evaluate_candidate(store, workspace: Path, candidate_path: Path, config: dict):\n    candidate=json.loads(candidate_path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    allow=set(config.get(\"evolution\",{}).get(\"allowlisted_keys\",[]))\n    changes=candidate.get(\"changes\",{})\n    illegal=[k for k in changes if k not in allow]\n    report={\"candidate\":candidate,\"illegal_keys\":illegal,\"score\":0.0,\n            \"passed\":not illegal and bool(changes),\"note\":\"V0.1 promotion gate is intentionally conservative; no code/provider/permission changes.\"}\n    exp_id=new_id(\"exp\")\n    with store.connect() as c:\n        c.execute(\"INSERT INTO experiments VALUES(?,?,?,?,?,?,?,?,?)\",\n                  (exp_id,None,candidate.get(\"reason\",\"Config candidate\"),json.dumps(candidate),\n                   0.0,0.0,\"rejected\" if illegal or not changes else \"review_required\",json.dumps(report),time.time()))\n    (workspace/\"experiments\").mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n    (workspace/\"experiments\"/f\"{exp_id}.json\").write_text(json.dumps(report,indent=2),encoding=\"utf-8\")\n    return report\n\"\"\",\n\"evoagent_comic/cli.py\": r\"\"\"\nimport argparse, json, shutil, sys\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom .config import load_config\nfrom .db import Store\nfrom .pipeline import ComicPipeline\nfrom .evaluation import evaluate_project\nfrom .evolution import evaluate_candidate\n\ndef main():\n    ap=argparse.ArgumentParser(prog=\"evo-comic\",description=\"EvoAgent Comic Studio MVP\")\n    sub=ap.add_subparsers(dest=\"cmd\",required=True)\n    p=sub.add_parser(\"init\"); p.add_argument(\"--workspace\",default=\"./workspace\")\n    p=sub.add_parser(\"run\"); p.add_argument(\"--workspace\",default=\"./workspace\"); p.add_argument(\"--title\",default=\"The Exiled Star\"); p.add_argument(\"--duration\",type=int,default=45); p.add_argument(\"--config\",default=\"config.toml\")\n    p=sub.add_parser(\"status\"); p.add_argument(\"--workspace\",default=\"./workspace\")\n    p=sub.add_parser(\"tasks\"); p.add_argument(\"--workspace\",default=\"./workspace\")\n    p=sub.add_parser(\"evaluate\"); p.add_argument(\"--workspace\",default=\"./workspace\"); p.add_argument(\"--project-id\")\n    p=sub.add_parser(\"evolve\"); p.add_argument(\"candidate\"); p.add_argument(\"--workspace\",default=\"./workspace\"); p.add_argument(\"--config\",default=\"config.toml\")\n    args=ap.parse_args()\n    workspace=Path(args.workspace).resolve()\n    if args.cmd==\"init\":\n        Store(workspace)\n        print(f\"Initialized workspace: {workspace}\")\n        print(\"Check that ffmpeg and ffprobe are installed before running a project.\")\n        return\n    store=Store(workspace)\n    if args.cmd==\"run\":\n        config=load_config(Path(args.config))\n        result=ComicPipeline(workspace,store,config).run(args.title,args.duration)\n        print(json.dumps(result,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))\n    elif args.cmd==\"status\":\n        print(json.dumps(store.projects(),ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))\n    elif args.cmd==\"tasks\":\n        print(json.dumps(store.tasks(),ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))\n    elif args.cmd==\"evaluate\":\n        projects=store.projects()\n        if args.project_id:\n            projects=[p for p in projects if p[\"project_id\"]==args.project_id]\n        out=[]\n        for p in projects:\n            matches=list((workspace/\"projects\").glob(f\"{p['project_id']}\"))\n            if matches: out.append(evaluate_project(matches[0]))\n        print(json.dumps(out,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))\n    elif args.cmd==\"evolve\":\n        config=load_config(Path(args.config))\n        print(json.dumps(evaluate_candidate(store,workspace,Path(args.candidate),config),ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))\n\nif __name__==\"__main__\": main()\n\"\"\",\n\"examples/candidate.json\": r\"\"\"\n{\n  \"reason\": \"Experiment: increase scene count for pacing\",\n  \"changes\": {\n    \"project.scene_count\": 4\n  }\n}\n\"\"\",\n\"docs/architecture.md\": r\"\"\"\n# Architecture notes\n\n## DAG\n\n1. `brief`: normalize user brief and constraints.\n2. `script`: generate story and dialogue.\n3. `character_bible`: freeze visual anchors and character metadata.\n4. `storyboard`: create shot-level prompts, durations, and dependencies.\n5. `scene_assets`: generate or retrieve scene media.\n6. `voice_assets`: generate voice audio per line/character.\n7. `subtitles`: align subtitle segments to actual audio durations.\n8. `assemble`: use FFmpeg to render the timeline.\n9. `quality_gate`: technical and semantic evaluation.\n10. `deliver`: publish a manifest and mark project complete.\n\n## Production DAG upgrades\n\nFor real providers, split `scene_assets` into per-shot tasks and `voice_assets` into per-line tasks. Use provider idempotency keys and persist remote job IDs before polling. A timeout must not blindly submit a second paid generation request.\n\n## Character consistency strategy\n\n- Create a canonical character bible with stable visual attributes.\n- Generate and approve reference sheets before scene generation.\n- Every shot request references the same character ID, reference asset IDs, outfit/state, and style bible.\n- Store prompt/version/provider/model/seed/reference assets for each output.\n- Compare each generated frame with references using image embeddings or a vision evaluator, but treat scores as a signal, not absolute truth.\n- Failed shots are regenerated individually; changes to a character bible mark dependent shots stale.\n\n## Budget strategy\n\nBefore every paid API call:\n1. Estimate worst-case cost and reserve it in the database.\n2. Check project and per-provider ceilings.\n3. Submit with an idempotency key.\n4. Reconcile provider-reported actual cost after completion.\n5. Release unused reservation.\n6. Stop or ask user if budget would be exceeded.\n\n## Quality strategy\n\nTechnical gates are deterministic: file existence, stream presence, duration, frame size, subtitle parse, audio loudness, black-frame checks, and A/V duration difference.\n\nSemantic gates require additional evaluators: character identity, shot continuity, dialogue-to-image alignment, narrative coherence, and policy/copyright review. Human approval is recommended before final publication in the MVP.\n\"\"\",\n\"docs/provider-contracts.md\": r\"\"\"\n# Provider adapter contracts\n\nImplement each provider as a separate adapter. Do not mix provider-specific HTTP code into the DAG runner.\n\n## Image provider\nInput: prompt, aspect ratio, character reference asset IDs, style profile, seed, idempotency key.\nOutput: asset path or remote asset URI, provider job ID, model ID, cost, dimensions, safety status.\n\n## Video provider\nInput: shot prompt, source keyframe(s), duration, aspect ratio, camera/motion direction, character reference, idempotency key.\nOutput: asset path/URI, actual duration, frame rate, job ID, model ID, cost, generation metadata.\n\n## TTS provider\nInput: text, voice ID, language, emotion, pace, pronunciation dictionary, idempotency key.\nOutput: audio path/URI, duration, sample rate, voice/model ID, cost, optional word timestamps.\n\n## LLM planner\nInput: normalized brief, character bible, scene budget, target duration.\nOutput: schema-validated JSON only; never executes tools directly.\n\"\"\",\n\"docs/acceptance.md\": r\"\"\"\n# MVP acceptance checklist\n\n## Local pipeline\n- [ ] Python 3.11+ and FFmpeg/ffprobe available.\n- [ ] `init` creates the workspace and database.\n- [ ] `run` creates project, assets, tasks, events, subtitles and final MP4.\n- [ ] Quality report confirms duration, video stream, audio stream and subtitle file.\n- [ ] Re-running creates a new project and does not overwrite prior project assets.\n\n## Failure handling\n- [ ] Missing FFmpeg records a failed task and issue.\n- [ ] Invalid duration is rejected before paid calls.\n- [ ] Failed task does not mark project succeeded.\n- [ ] Budget reservation prevents a paid call that would exceed the budget (must be wired into each real provider adapter).\n- [ ] Provider timeout uses idempotency and does not create duplicate paid jobs.\n\n## Production readiness beyond V0.1\n- [ ] Real image/video/TTS providers integrated and tested.\n- [ ] Semantic visual consistency evaluator.\n- [ ] Audio loudness and subtitle synchronization checks.\n- [ ] Authentication, secret management, rate limiting, and job queue.\n- [ ] Android API and release manifest integration.\n\"\"\",\n}\nfor rel, content in files.items():\n    path = root / rel\n    path.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n    path.write_text(textwrap.dedent(content).lstrip(), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n# create test file\ntest_content = r'''\nimport tempfile, unittest\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom evoagent_comic.dag import DagNode, DagRunner\n\nclass DagTests(unittest.TestCase):\n    def test_topological_order(self):\n        ran=[]\n        runner=DagRunner([\n            DagNode(\"b\",[\"a\"],lambda: ran.append(\"b\") or {}),\n            DagNode(\"a\",[],lambda: ran.append(\"a\") or {})\n        ])\n        runner.run()\n        self.assertEqual(ran,[\"a\",\"b\"])\n\n    def test_cycle_rejected(self):\n        runner=DagRunner([\n            DagNode(\"a\",[\"b\"],lambda:{}),\n            DagNode(\"b\",[\"a\"],lambda:{})\n        ])\n        with self.assertRaises(ValueError):\n            runner.order()\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    unittest.main()\n'''\n(root/\"tests\").mkdir(exist_ok=True)\n(root/\"tests/test_dag.py\").write_text(textwrap.dedent(test_content).lstrip(), encoding=\"utf-8\")\n\n# config docs\nzip_path = Path(\"/mnt/data/evoagent-comic-studio-v0.1.zip\")\nif zip_path.exists():\n    zip_path.unlink()\nwith zipfile.ZipFile(zip_path, \"w\", zipfile.ZIP_DEFLATED) as z:\n    for p in root.rglob(\"*\"):\n        if p.is_file():\n            z.write(p, p.relative_to(root.parent))\nprint(f\"Created {zip_path} with {sum(1 for p in root.rglob('*') if p.is_file())} files\")\n"},"status":"finished_successfully","end_turn":false,"weight":1.0,"metadata":{"finish_details":{"type":"stop","stop_tokens":[200012]},"is_complete":true,"citations":[],"content_references":[],"gizmo_id":"g-p-6ad449077a8c8191825a8ee19d54ef7a","cot_version":"v5","request_id":"3f6b3021-f249-4ac9-90cb-b11c69cd445f","message_type":"next","turn_exchange_id":"ce6ec6a2-5bbc-4770-906e-33ca35cdb639","working_turn_id":"ce6ec6a2-5bbc-4770-906e-33ca35cdb639","model_slug":"gpt-6","default_model_slug":"gpt-6","parent_id":"8e73e884-ca53-49b7-bd26-fe28b7930327","model_switcher_deny":[],"can_save":false},"recipient":"python","channel":"commentary"}],"safe_urls":["https://developer.android.com/reference/android/accessibilityservice/AccessibilityService?aut